  "reconstructibility": 1,
  "reason": "The records collectively establish several important ingredients: powder-based consolidation of refractory HEAs near 1400 °C, additive manufacture with in-situ alloying from mixed powders, strong interstitial O/N strengthening in the Hf-Nb-Ta-Ti-Zr family, cooling-dependent suppression of phase decomposition, and oxidation resistance from protective oxides. R1 is particularly strong evidence for oxygen strengthening in the exact HfNbTaTiZr system, while R20 supports interstitial strengthening in a nearly identical alloy and R15 supports rapid-cooling suppression of decomposition. However, none discloses hydride-bearing printable ink, hydrogen de-binding, sequential hydride decomposition according to formation enthalpy, titanium-sponge oxygen gettering, or a self-healing silicide coating. Thus the literature points in the right direction, but combining these elements into the later paper's specific intervention would require substantial new ideas."
